Based on the taxonomy and the provided HTML, the following semantic accessibility violation was detected:

1. **Affected HTML Element:**
[START]
<html><head><style>
		.notInPage {
			position: absolute;
			left: -9999px;
			top: -9999px;
		}
	</style>
	</head><body>
		<button class="notInPage">Save</button>

</body></html>
[END]

* **Violation Name:** `page-title-not-descriptive`
* **Description:** The HTML document completely lacks a `<title>` element in the `<head>`, meaning there is no page title to describe the content or purpose of the page to assistive technology users.
